  "body": "A tilted (3+2) 2D Contour with \"Do not touch\" gets a `rapid_in_part` finding that the same Contour without protection does not get.\n\nFound during the work on #3344.\n\n## Steps\n\nThe pin `contour::contour_do_not_touch_keeps_full_tool_clear_of_protected_face_and_edge` (`crates/app/tests/do_not_touch/contour.rs`, tilted case) sets up:\n\n1. The plate and tower fixture of `do_not_touch_support`, with the tower at `[44, 0, 0]`.\n2. A 2D Contour on the plate: top Z 8, bottom Z 3, stepdown 5, tilt `a_deg` 5.\n3. The tower top face as a protected item, clearance 1.0.\n\n## What happens\n\n- Without protection, `verify` gives three `gouge` findings. The plate walls stand 5 degrees off the tool axis.\n- With protection, `verify` gives no `avoid_hit`. It gives `rapid_in_part` on move 1 and more `gouge` findings.\n- The post is blocked in the two cases. No wrong G-code is posted.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Find which avoid step moves the first rapid of the tilted path into the part (link routing or the clipped-piece entry).\n2. Make the protected path add no finding kind that the plain path does not have.\n3. Add that assertion to the tilted case of the pin.\n\nRefs #3344.\n",
